extends ../layouts/docs

block variables
    - const pageTitle = 'API reference';
    - const currentPage = 'api-reference';
    - const description = 'Reference for the template build commands and source/output paths; no public HTTP or JavaScript API is provided.';

block content
    h2#api-scope Public API scope
    p This template exposes no HTTP API or public JavaScript API. #[code src/js/scripts.js] is intentionally empty apart from comments. There are no service endpoints, authentication tokens, or request/response schemas to configure.
    p The reference below describes the npm build interface and file layout. Functions inside #[code scripts/] are implementation details, not a stable library API.
    h2#commands npm commands
    p Run these commands from the repository root after #[code npm ci].
    dl
        dt #[code npm run build]
        dd Cleans the output, then builds Pug, SCSS, scripts, and assets in sequence.
        dt #[code npm run clean]
        dd Deletes #[code dist/]. Back up any direct output edits before running it.
        dt #[code npm run build:pug]
        dd Compiles Pug pages into HTML; layouts and include/mixin files are excluded as standalone pages. This does not clean stale output or build CSS/assets.
        dt #[code npm run build:scss]
        dd Compiles #[code src/scss/styles.scss], including Bootstrap, into #[code dist/css/styles.css].
        dt #[code npm run build:scripts]
        dd Copies #[code src/js/] into #[code dist/js/] and adds the template banner to #[code scripts.js].
        dt #[code npm run build:assets]
        dd Copies #[code src/assets/] into #[code dist/assets/].
        dt #[code npm start]
        dd Builds, watches source files, and runs a local BrowserSync preview.
        dt #[code npm run start:debug]
        dd Builds and launches the project's debug-mode preview workflow.
        dt #[code npm run test:docs]
        dd Checks existing generated documentation. Run a build first after changing source.
        dt #[code npm test]
        dd Builds the site and runs the documentation check.
    h2#paths Source and output contracts
    ul
        li #[code src/pug/index.pug] becomes #[code dist/index.html].
        li #[code src/pug/docs/*.pug] becomes corresponding #[code dist/docs/*.html] files.
        li #[code src/pug/layouts/docs.pug] is shared by documentation pages and does not become a standalone page.
        li #[code src/scss/styles.scss] becomes #[code dist/css/styles.css].
        li #[code src/js/] and #[code src/assets/] are copied into the matching output directories.
    p Preserve this output structure when publishing. The complete build is the supported way to remove stale generated files after deleting or renaming a page.
